{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_961c61992ada0344410e800c40e28c0dba89321eb1d6f0e8647ac8668b522ca7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors need Node.js >=20, npm or yarn, GNU Make, and Python >=3.10 with pip for pre-commit; setup uses make install and make setup-hooks, with make test, make lint, and make format for tests, linting, and formatting."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fa8e555c95cc622f060d8ed2a85c5b1a3671bee907b7bec601b04ff3b47da8bd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: pull requests should have all tests passing and a clear change description, and submission implies licensing contributions under the project's license."}],"claim_ids":["clm_961c61992ada0344410e800c40e28c0dba89321eb1d6f0e8647ac8668b522ca7","clm_fa8e555c95cc622f060d8ed2a85c5b1a3671bee907b7bec601b04ff3b47da8bd"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:42:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f55958eea0e4a3e9121d59ab317d1bf","id":"pg_58d76e17f2fc50d98ebddef20ba9ac1b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/cogitatortech-binharic-cli-contributing-md-52ccca70bdad-def20ba9ac1b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_a423a24c20cd54ea8c0f1a91dc9a1105"],"title":"CogitatorTech/binharic-cli/CONTRIBUTING.md @ 52ccca70bdad","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:42:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f55958eea0e4a3e9121d59ab317d1bf"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0a7b6de554c258f32c18c631c3c20e806aee9f5ef28226d6a280de51b5ba2d60"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration is done via the ~/.config/binharic/config.json5 file, and environment variables are also supported for configuration."},{"claim_ids":["clm_18c50b72d9123ea51d53be3fb79454c694eb7450885887748382c855e40195a4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented features include models from OpenAI, Google, Anthropic, and Ollama; a keyword-based RAG pipeline; built-in tools for file reading and Bash commands; and MCP-based external tools."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2cc10d005820d402676175a8ba9fcb9644c521314f5c3f30c96efbefcefda56b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is MIT-licensed, published on npm, and positions itself as a general-purpose coding agent able to analyze projects, run tests, find bugs, and perform code review."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3ec46cb45c1bcd26af6b4dc981554e100dc97fbe14ef87b1d2ee1713dd0a7879"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture reportedly follows recommendations from Anthropic's 'building effective agents' article to a good degree."},{"claim_ids":["clm_532165133fb109047382f4333d8581b2b904206d7f352374f0530bf4dc611ec0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states Binharic is in early development, so bugs and breaking changes are expected."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8cd44cb541843f568717e5cff92150ffbeded0639e94da8c6af4c99ff7e97b3b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is written in TypeScript and uses the AI SDK framework for much of its agentic logic such as tool calling and workflow management."},{"claim_ids":["clm_93df243fd0776a85038cecb6efd0e0e9235b2d2a96fe34e8403fceec5d96ea59"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Binharic is a terminal-based AI coding assistant with the persona of a Tech-Priest of the Adeptus Mechanicus, comparable to Codex, Gemini CLI, and Claude Code."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9fb38b8298be70b9dca5051fb4211d968b51a37d9903d76a678c4d839cf7cf14"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Users install the npm package @cogitator/binharic-cli globally and launch the agent with the 'binharic' command in a terminal."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b45b67a03f6146c5c26ee10da5261417333507217ddfc0780cac5837812b2ae4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A Docker image is published to GitHub Container Registry with multi-arch builds (linux/amd64 and linux/arm64), and the agent can be run in a container mounting the working directory at /workspace."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fa7636a79bf5f4f2d2facca4b7a82f9ab91b04e133a340938a3c476bac1b788c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"API keys for OpenAI, Anthropic, and Google are supplied through environment variables when running the agent."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0a7b6de554c258f32c18c631c3c20e806aee9f5ef28226d6a280de51b5ba2d60","clm_18c50b72d9123ea51d53be3fb79454c694eb7450885887748382c855e40195a4","clm_2cc10d005820d402676175a8ba9fcb9644c521314f5c3f30c96efbefcefda56b","clm_3ec46cb45c1bcd26af6b4dc981554e100dc97fbe14ef87b1d2ee1713dd0a7879","clm_532165133fb109047382f4333d8581b2b904206d7f352374f0530bf4dc611ec0","clm_8cd44cb541843f568717e5cff92150ffbeded0639e94da8c6af4c99ff7e97b3b","clm_93df243fd0776a85038cecb6efd0e0e9235b2d2a96fe34e8403fceec5d96ea59","clm_9fb38b8298be70b9dca5051fb4211d968b51a37d9903d76a678c4d839cf7cf14","clm_b45b67a03f6146c5c26ee10da5261417333507217ddfc0780cac5837812b2ae4","clm_fa7636a79bf5f4f2d2facca4b7a82f9ab91b04e133a340938a3c476bac1b788c"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:42:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f55958eea0e4a3e9121d59ab317d1bf","id":"pg_5bdda38cf66f53389009fc9b507b2674","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/cogitatortech-binharic-cli-readme-md-52ccca70bdad-fc9b507b2674.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_633bf2f81c4a5d0789c9720fa188ae1b"],"title":"CogitatorTech/binharic-cli/README.md @ 52ccca70bdad","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:42:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f55958eea0e4a3e9121d59ab317d1bf"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_016b43cca18f3d98c016d24052c5cb12c699927d5f17f0f66b8de299241c6335"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The roadmap marks sandboxed tool execution, encrypted configuration files, rate limiting, and audit logging as not yet implemented."},{"claim_ids":["clm_45e69ce012351ffdd9d64e6b731691b3814fff5784e9bda2ed0fb18744ce33f2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The roadmap marks as implemented a main Tech-Priest agent plus specialized agents such as a Code Analysis Agent and a Security agent."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4ee0adc5b15e2d4d619cd077ef57337933da2ce88d4e53792154f30a91e594f4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The roadmap lists a tool execution confirmation flow and tool execution timeout protection (10 seconds for autofix) as implemented, while sandboxed tool execution remains unchecked."},{"claim_ids":["clm_578c93f78aea6f58fdd729694d388e67f2459d6ff52a46083c6438c916979085"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The roadmap lists implemented multi-step tool calling with retry logic, transient error handling with exponential backoff, tool execution confirmation, and error/completion-based stopping conditions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b45b67a03f6146c5c26ee10da5261417333507217ddfc0780cac5837812b2ae4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A Docker image is published to GitHub Container Registry with multi-arch builds (linux/amd64 and linux/arm64), and the agent can be run in a container mounting the working directory at /workspace."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c828ac96ed8334853b857db406980d148e80fddd00df22b4a583de951da18e1a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Implemented context management includes token-based context window management, automatic trimming for long conversations, history preservation across sessions, and tool result summarization."}],"claim_ids":["clm_016b43cca18f3d98c016d24052c5cb12c699927d5f17f0f66b8de299241c6335","clm_45e69ce012351ffdd9d64e6b731691b3814fff5784e9bda2ed0fb18744ce33f2","clm_4ee0adc5b15e2d4d619cd077ef57337933da2ce88d4e53792154f30a91e594f4","clm_578c93f78aea6f58fdd729694d388e67f2459d6ff52a46083c6438c916979085","clm_b45b67a03f6146c5c26ee10da5261417333507217ddfc0780cac5837812b2ae4","clm_c828ac96ed8334853b857db406980d148e80fddd00df22b4a583de951da18e1a"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:42:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f55958eea0e4a3e9121d59ab317d1bf","id":"pg_9ce3e7587a845c17aff1777a61805111","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/cogitatortech-binharic-cli-roadmap-md-52ccca70bdad-777a61805111.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_a13690349dac5ab0aef25d91c64c7e07"],"title":"CogitatorTech/binharic-cli/ROADMAP.md @ 52ccca70bdad","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:42:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f55958eea0e4a3e9121d59ab317d1bf"}
